      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! Residents often express concerns about potential increases in traffic, parking shortages, and pressure on local infrastructure. They worry that the project's height might overshadow historical architecture and that it may change the character of the neighborhood. There’s also fear that it's too large, leading to a lesser sense of community. It’s good to anticipate these points in your proposal.",
      "source": "target",
